{"data": [{"author_id": "14724354", "created_at": "2026-10-30T10:25:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116114221809193227"], "id": "2116114221809193227", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Hooked on Grok Bot. I run a crew of bots, each with its own job, and spend my day herding them: renaming, rewriting instructions, correcting course. Dangerously addictive.\n\nIn Spain it's the only always-on agent I can use. Dot, Duet and the rest aren't available to me yet. I'd", "url": "https://x.com/Nephel/status/2116114221809193227"}, {"author_id": "2001430393938153473", "created_at": "2026-10-30T07:11:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116065416896524462"], "id": "2116065416896524462", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2001430393938153473", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116065348067934471", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ajambrosino Dots is promising, but too often it delegates work, sends routine blockers back to me, and reports activity without verifying the actual outcome. An always-on agent should take ownership of results, not just dispatch tasks. (3/6)", "url": "https://x.com/hachimi6250/status/2116065416896524462"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116056372597125120", "3_2116056372609728512"]}, "author_id": "2356425306", "created_at": "2026-10-30T06:57:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116061894587056182"], "id": "2116061894587056182", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Rex \u5b8c\u6210\u5ea6\u8fd8\u662f\u633a\u9ad8\u7684\uff0c\u6f02\u4eae\u3001\u4f53\u9a8c\u4e5f\u4e1d\u6ed1\u3002\u53ef\u4ee5\u76f4\u63a5\u8fdb\u884c Terminal \u7684\u8fdc\u7a0b\u63a7\u5236\u548c\u88ab\u63a7\uff0c\u4e5f\u5bf9 Agent CLI \u505a\u4e86\u4f18\u5316\u548c\u96c6\u6210\uff0c\u4f1a\u662f\u4e00\u4e2a\u4e0d\u9519\u7684\u65b0\u7ec8\u7aef\u9009\u62e9\u3002\n\nAlways-On Agent \u9010\u6e10\u6210\u4e3a\u4e3b\u6d41\uff0c\u5927\u5bb6\u5bf9\u4ed6\u7684\u7ba1\u7406\u4e5f\u8d8b\u5411\u4e8e\u4e09\u8005\uff1aRemote Terminal\u3001Remote Client\u3001\u5e73\u53f0\u5316\u7edf\u4e00\u7ba1\u7406\uff0c\u8bf8\u5982 Mosh\u3001Lody \u548c Grok Bot https://t.co/qKsiLva4CK", "url": "https://x.com/txperl/status/2116061894587056182"}, {"author_id": "1037725470630891520", "created_at": "2026-10-30T05:37:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116041682236109256"], "id": "2116041682236109256", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2044061881325797376", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116031752225341933", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Organic_Release Depends on the job: Claude for long tool-calling chains, a cheaper fast model for simple routing steps. If you want to see how a finished always-on agent behaves, my invite gives you 2 weeks of Grok Bot free (accounts new to Grok):\nhttps://t.co/Mznq32dnzi", "url": "https://x.com/johnherzog/status/2116041682236109256"}, {"author_id": "1037725470630891520", "created_at": "2026-10-30T05:03:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116033207095448047"], "id": "2116033207095448047", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2020894476848558080", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 81, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115998954181816694", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@tec_safwan Solid list, the assistants section alone is worth the bookmark. I'd add Grok Bot, an always-on agent with its own computer. Anyone curious can grab a free 2-week trial with my invite (accounts new to Grok only):\nhttps://t.co/Mznq32dnzi", "url": "https://x.com/johnherzog/status/2116033207095448047"}, {"auth